*.sh text eol=lf
test/** text eol=lf
.github/** text eol=lf

# Runnable example configs a reader may copy straight onto a Linux host: keep
# them LF so a CRLF checkout on a Windows clone cannot ship broken snapshots.
docs/examples/*.conf text eol=lf

# The two GENERATED protocol views. reviewctl.sh writes LF and --verify compares
# byte for byte, so a checkout that rewrites them to CRLF makes the ledger look
# hand-edited on every Windows clone -- a false alarm about the one file whose
# whole purpose is to be trustworthy.
docs/internal/reviews/REVIEW_LEDGER.md text eol=lf
docs/project/OPEN-THREADS.md text eol=lf

# Everything reviewctl PARSES, not just the two views it writes.
#
# The views were pinned when a CRLF checkout made --verify's byte comparison
# fail. The inputs were not, and that is worse than a failing comparison: a
# machine header is matched by a pattern anchored to `-->` at end of line, so on
# a CRLF clone the line ends `-->\r`, the header is silently INVISIBLE, and the
# Windows implementer derives a different review state than CI does -- quietly,
# with no error. Measured 2026-08-14: a delivery recorded in DELIVERIES.md was
# open on Linux and absent locally, and only the PR check disagreed.
docs/internal/reviews/**/*.md text eol=lf
docs/project/DELIVERIES.md text eol=lf
